+## 2026-09-08 — Blocker handoff certification
+
+The integrated target `9fde0baa9fbae768fc97133731eeb2744f90516e` was
+certified after it had been committed; certification was recorded later in
+`b9764a6a`. The isolated historical target `820221a9` remains rejected: its lock
+named six files while four role files were absent, its committed config did not
+match the lock, and the checker and G19 guard wiring were absent. The first
+certification reviewer discovered that dependency-boundary defect and blocked
+the initial certification attempt.
+
+The human resolved the boundary through repair commits `07e1d466`, `51689ecd`,
+`e111957b`, and `9fde0baa`. The human root-cause finding is composition: each
+loop correctly committed only its allowed paths, but a lock landed without its
+referents; no isolated loop failed. This finding remains separate from the two
+historical deviations. DEVIATION A is the difference between the approved T01
+Accept containing `Para humanos` and both recorded executions containing
+`For humans`; approval-time SPEC bytes or an original-command artifact, editor,
+edit time, and the cause distinguishing runner substitution from a SPEC edit are
+not recorded. DEVIATION B is the
+absence of final dual independent approvals in the predecessor record.
+
+Decision: exact approved gates and two independent approvals over the same
+unchanged state are required for certification. Missing evidence stays visible
+instead of being inferred or reconstructed, because configuration intent and
+later prose do not prove the state that actually ran. The two later T02 reviews
+certify integrated `9fde0baa` only; they do not retroactively approve the
+predecessor tasks or rehabilitate isolated `820221a9`.
